sentences.l:
“Tydeus’-son Diomedes, made welcome to my heart,
neither do you, at least, fear Ares on that account, nor any other
of the immortals: such a helper to you am I;

And when they were near, going against one another,
in front Ares reached out over the yoke and the reins of the horses
with his bronze spear, eager to take away his life;
